WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:02.230
So napping is super important.

2
00:00:02.580 --> 00:00:03.980
It's important for athletes

3
00:00:03.980 --> 00:00:06.670
and it's important for the general population.

4
00:00:07.160 --> 00:00:09.080
If you're able to take

5
00:00:09.080 --> 00:00:12.480
even a 15, 20-minute nap,

6
00:00:12.480 --> 00:00:14.820
power nap has been shown

7
00:00:14.820 --> 00:00:19.530
to increase levels of alertness, boost mood.

8
00:00:20.580 --> 00:00:21.820
And even in those people

9
00:00:21.820 --> 00:00:24.120
who are getting a good amount

10
00:00:24.120 --> 00:00:25.170
of sleep at night,

11
00:00:25.320 --> 00:00:26.540
the naps have been shown

12
00:00:26.540 --> 00:00:30.120
to be even more beneficial for them as well

13
00:00:30.120 --> 00:00:33.740
as far as with regard to productivity

14
00:00:33.740 --> 00:00:35.550
and alertness, et cetera.

15
00:00:35.960 --> 00:00:37.750
So napping is important.

16
00:00:38.360 --> 00:00:41.730
We recommend about a 20-minute nap.

17
00:00:41.920 --> 00:00:43.120
So you would set your alarm

18
00:00:43.120 --> 00:00:44.710
for about 30 minutes.

19
00:00:45.300 --> 00:00:49.410
And then, you know, if your alarm goes off,

20
00:00:49.500 --> 00:00:51.370
if you wake up before your alarm,

21
00:00:51.460 --> 00:00:53.590
certainly get up.

22
00:00:54.060 --> 00:00:56.100
And then the timing of the nap

23
00:00:56.100 --> 00:00:57.940
is important as well.

24
00:00:57.940 --> 00:00:59.120
So we don't want to nap

25
00:00:59.120 --> 00:01:00.790
too close to bedtime.

26
00:01:01.660 --> 00:01:04.490
So aiming for between noon and 4 p.m.

27
00:01:05.060 --> 00:01:07.370
is a good kind of range.

28
00:01:08.140 --> 00:01:09.560
And then for those athletes

29
00:01:09.560 --> 00:01:12.420
or for those people who may not be getting

30
00:01:12.420 --> 00:01:13.970
enough sleep at night,

31
00:01:14.540 --> 00:01:15.410
so for example,

32
00:01:15.500 --> 00:01:18.090
a swimmer who has a 5 a.m.,

33
00:01:18.380 --> 00:01:19.000
or, you know,

34
00:01:19.000 --> 00:01:20.190
has to get up at 5 a.m.,

35
00:01:20.480 --> 00:01:22.000
it's likely that they're not able

36
00:01:22.000 --> 00:01:23.410
to get enough sleep at night.

37
00:01:23.740 --> 00:01:25.280
So extending that nap

38
00:01:25.280 --> 00:01:27.370
to no more than two hours

39
00:01:28.360 --> 00:01:29.780
is important for them

40
00:01:29.780 --> 00:01:31.060
to make up some of that

41
00:01:31.060 --> 00:01:32.750
lost sleep at night.
